    "result_text": "The full suite passes \u2014 21 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` feature. When a create request sets `sharesHousehold: true`, an owner is now allowed at an address already used by a same-last-name owner, and all owners in that household are assigned the same stable `householdId`, which is returned on the owner record.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `householdId` property to the `Owner` schema, so it appears on `OwnerDto` and is returned by `GET /api/owners/{id}` (the generated DTO/mapper picks it up automatically).\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `householdId` field (`@Column(name = \"household_id\")`) with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it into `OwnerDto` by name (same as the existing `customerCode`).\n\n3. **`db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 Added the `household_id` column to the `owners` table in every DB dialect (tests load the schema explicitly via `spring.sql.init`).\n\n4. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014\n   - Refactored `isHouseholdDuplicate` into `findHouseholdMembers`, which returns the existing owners matching the normalized last name + address.\n   - When `sharesHousehold` is true **and** a matching household already exists, the create is allowed (existing behavior) and now also derives a stable `householdId` \u2014 a deterministic `HH-<SHA-256 prefix>` of the normalized last name + address \u2014 assigning it to the new owner and back-filling it onto existing household members that don't yet have one. Being deterministic, every co-resident resolves to the same value regardless of creation order.\n\nThe `householdId` is only assigned in the household-sharing scenario; ordinary owners leave it null.\n\nNote: the test run executes against **HSQLDB** (`jdbc:hsqldb:mem:petclinic`) via the test profile, and the schema change there was necessary for the column to exist. All 21 tests pass, including `Cp11Tests.coreJoinersShareHouseholdId` and the existing `Cp10Tests`.",
